      "id": "thm-reparameterization-gradient-under-dominated-differentiation",
      "location": "Facts & Assumptions [F5]",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The entry says the chain rule means “the encoder gradient differentiates through the fixed-noise map.” But `def-pathwise-simulation-gradient-estimator` gives its componentwise chain-rule formula only when the inner map and outer payoff are differentiable. This theorem assumes only that the full payoff H_i is C1; it does not assume g_phi or the separate log-density factors are differentiable. For example, g(φ)=|φ| and h(z)=z² give a C1 composite H(φ)=φ² although g is not differentiable at 0. Thus the full-payoff derivative assumption does not license the stated componentwise inference.",
